[{:db/id "q-162418/selection/ebb334501c2650e4735a66058396c133960cee3a478c7128b11a2e64e5547b79" :answer/id #uuid "0461dd71-d8cd-5ecf-ab88-b96bb43e7e5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162418/selection/43a429515e6847f2a52bfbd156c03ec3124d669d88446b81e64c7bd58a0ed1cc" :answer/id #uuid "c0c8e624-13a2-53ac-b199-d1630e743323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162418/selection/355c0dd52bb99a600c16fa827ff5e6c8c906aa844b1a693f42112fc4e3e0de20" :answer/id #uuid "432453a7-04a6-5db9-9b15-158a97e066b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162418/selection/c0bf3250d4d52b272ca6792361dbb8d89222f7e1a2fce8185212b5e8a0066620" :answer/id #uuid "c221d7e7-f01e-5b7f-bb68-27bf6b9a8edf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162418/selection/3b55008aebee697f6217a9828d70c420c582fba56cbd7b6cbd6f1e97b640273b" :answer/id #uuid "153ba1ed-f753-568a-aa19-42467ed2f998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162418/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3534edc-1576-5295-90d1-b7cc5e0bf56b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162418/selection/c0bf3250d4d52b272ca6792361dbb8d89222f7e1a2fce8185212b5e8a0066620" :answer-field/choices ["q-162418/selection/ebb334501c2650e4735a66058396c133960cee3a478c7128b11a2e64e5547b79" "q-162418/selection/43a429515e6847f2a52bfbd156c03ec3124d669d88446b81e64c7bd58a0ed1cc" "q-162418/selection/355c0dd52bb99a600c16fa827ff5e6c8c906aa844b1a693f42112fc4e3e0de20" "q-162418/selection/c0bf3250d4d52b272ca6792361dbb8d89222f7e1a2fce8185212b5e8a0066620" "q-162418/selection/3b55008aebee697f6217a9828d70c420c582fba56cbd7b6cbd6f1e97b640273b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162418" :question/id #uuid "ac9e9607-a2dd-5594-94f3-d6c7ba9a234a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162418" :question/problem "The signed curvature of the plane curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-{t}^{2}⟩$ is given by\n\n$$\nk(t)=\\frac{2\\cdot (\\,\\,)}{\\sqrt{({cos}^{2}⁡t+4{t}^{2})^{3}}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" :question/worked-solution "The signed curvature $k(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$ is given by\n\n$$\nk(t)=\\frac{{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y(t)=-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-2t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the signed curvature, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(t) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-2)-(-2t)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}{{((\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(-2t)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{{({cos}^{2}⁡t+4{t}^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}{\\sqrt{({cos}^{2}⁡t+4{t}^{2})^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162418/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "814655d8-f459-5df5-b722-3024b87065db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162418"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162387/selection/31892fd407b41f6721548753b143307078ab3da16b9842008e83f07f9401ff08" :answer/id #uuid "a9b23674-bf2a-5d7d-8be7-8efeb0b3346d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{(1+4{t}^{2}+4t)}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162387/selection/2f8822d277f6ca0bf6b74e6e52e370037dd5d0b52d7681dddda52c0b306495a9" :answer/id #uuid "a0927d8a-287b-54d7-8453-1b8762f3b287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{(1+{t}^{2}+{t}^{4})}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162387/selection/e094ffc884e3ac5592da9a046521b6c1679e717821515007f79e1cb32e8a023e" :answer/id #uuid "3ad4766b-ad92-5cda-a884-564b6a2fda18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{(2t+{t}^{4})}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162387/selection/a8a065b9a01724325f9b9e9095303e52a7f1354a459ac4b0752389028ff2b728" :answer/id #uuid "a7e7d0b0-9af6-52e8-9396-6b48417925ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162387/selection/7fdaa2c425ee76a4680179b548d9bd22693717c2efd4fa3e159c88cae490a5ea" :answer/id #uuid "9881ef89-bffe-52bc-98b1-2e975109141e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{(1+4{t}^{4})}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162387/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f20d1866-ad62-5792-a608-3b8f787fdf2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162387/selection/a8a065b9a01724325f9b9e9095303e52a7f1354a459ac4b0752389028ff2b728" :answer-field/choices ["q-162387/selection/31892fd407b41f6721548753b143307078ab3da16b9842008e83f07f9401ff08" "q-162387/selection/2f8822d277f6ca0bf6b74e6e52e370037dd5d0b52d7681dddda52c0b306495a9" "q-162387/selection/e094ffc884e3ac5592da9a046521b6c1679e717821515007f79e1cb32e8a023e" "q-162387/selection/a8a065b9a01724325f9b9e9095303e52a7f1354a459ac4b0752389028ff2b728" "q-162387/selection/7fdaa2c425ee76a4680179b548d9bd22693717c2efd4fa3e159c88cae490a5ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162387" :question/id #uuid "6c665a10-c572-5402-ab7b-5950f84379a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-162387" :question/problem "The curvature of the plane curve $r(t)=-t\\,i+({t}^{2}+1)\\,j$ is given by \n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{2}{}.\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=-t,\\,y(t)={t}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-1,\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =2t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =0,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2-2t\\cdot 0|}{{((-1)^{2}+(2t)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2|}{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{(1+4{t}^{2})}^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162387/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "814655d8-f459-5df5-b722-3024b87065db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162387"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162414/selection/04ec84d31a7c05b42c6c3384daa13c5db3ecdbd0a2bdd4e779511157dbaf110b" :answer/id #uuid "480d11da-0304-5f72-9e44-cc11c21f408d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{({sin}^{2}⁡t+1)}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162414/selection/4521436769afbadd05c9fffb13081c5e5e919e19cbbcf115c8471d164c13b56b" :answer/id #uuid "acd2afb4-791a-5273-9ec8-1489af6925f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{({sin}^{2}⁡t+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162414/selection/58e5e8e790300504970753a93f8bb01f8763f158babeee5fd31a4952073e7dcf" :answer/id #uuid "a6088312-994d-5ff9-aa95-62aa9cbed6ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{({sin}^{3}⁡t+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162414/selection/8e6b5e4d8f6e14d981a1a44eb8a4244792da49d3c4258b44fb419bda669c12f9" :answer/id #uuid "4120ca89-3312-54b6-a72e-5a2667153757" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162414/selection/e1a401c8a8263c6692cc1a97545a7c61d80cf43f041a7618674844982086cba5" :answer/id #uuid "4216f520-5c3b-51cc-b477-b6f8062a8454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+1)}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162414/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f678ce1b-c920-5d24-ac8e-31117f181720" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162414/selection/04ec84d31a7c05b42c6c3384daa13c5db3ecdbd0a2bdd4e779511157dbaf110b" :answer-field/choices ["q-162414/selection/04ec84d31a7c05b42c6c3384daa13c5db3ecdbd0a2bdd4e779511157dbaf110b" "q-162414/selection/4521436769afbadd05c9fffb13081c5e5e919e19cbbcf115c8471d164c13b56b" "q-162414/selection/58e5e8e790300504970753a93f8bb01f8763f158babeee5fd31a4952073e7dcf" "q-162414/selection/8e6b5e4d8f6e14d981a1a44eb8a4244792da49d3c4258b44fb419bda669c12f9" "q-162414/selection/e1a401c8a8263c6692cc1a97545a7c61d80cf43f041a7618674844982086cba5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162414" :question/id #uuid "d5ac123c-3663-55fc-a172-6e4b0415bb6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162414" :question/problem "The curvature of the plane curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\,j$ is given by \n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{},\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(t)=t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 0-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot 1|}{{((\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{1}^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|}{{({sin}^{2}⁡t+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\sqrt{{({sin}^{2}⁡t+1)}^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we removed the absolute value because cosine is positive for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162414/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "814655d8-f459-5df5-b722-3024b87065db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162414"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162420/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" :answer/id #uuid "e86dbb41-3190-5cb1-a2b5-14132394dd1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162420/selection/bdb344504abc3a20477be3b0061a467b51fce04e586ae596a6ef1bbf0033c4ee" :answer/id #uuid "bcae384f-f753-5504-8ca1-7997b4f47cde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162420/selection/bef6371d4584cb4dd48eaa50d1a6755e653e4027f2c5f5b658f261ff528e8e35" :answer/id #uuid "8cab9783-92c5-58db-8e0b-aa3265f50d03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162420/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" :answer/id #uuid "0821b046-a964-5bff-855e-605d4f6050ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162420/selection/df4b6fddd29d1c2f1c0e7bf5f78b46b82bd28351da59a114b28fc29f920b14b5" :answer/id #uuid "f3019d67-05d3-589c-8b07-d2b4cb5298cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162420/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "61f3ce2a-308f-5c39-9f74-d69b72339b85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162420/selection/bdb344504abc3a20477be3b0061a467b51fce04e586ae596a6ef1bbf0033c4ee" :answer-field/choices ["q-162420/selection/b4ac6936776440214aaebffba73d7fd5fde48538e542fa8a6de8788032995d2c" "q-162420/selection/bdb344504abc3a20477be3b0061a467b51fce04e586ae596a6ef1bbf0033c4ee" "q-162420/selection/bef6371d4584cb4dd48eaa50d1a6755e653e4027f2c5f5b658f261ff528e8e35" "q-162420/selection/cb9ad14c4d0189695cf5d02baf58f5eec7ac941edc170f6dffed142cbab880f5" "q-162420/selection/df4b6fddd29d1c2f1c0e7bf5f78b46b82bd28351da59a114b28fc29f920b14b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162420" :question/id #uuid "b2299202-b673-50d0-ad04-bb6f2463ec0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-162420" :question/problem "The signed curvature of the plane curve $r(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,t⟩$ is given by\n\n$$\nk(t)=\\frac{}{\\sqrt{(1+{t}^{2})^{3}}},\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" :question/worked-solution "The signed curvature $k(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$ is given by\n\n$$\nk(t)=\\frac{{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,y(t)=t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-{t}^{-1},\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & ={t}^{-2},\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the signed curvature, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(t) & =\\frac{-{t}^{-1}\\cdot 0-1\\cdot ({t}^{-2})}{{((-{t}^{-1})^{2}+(1)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{t}^{-2}}{{({t}^{-2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{t}^{-2}\\cdot ({t}^{2})^{3/2}}{{(1+{t}^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{t}^{-2}\\cdot |t{|}^{3}}{{(1+{t}^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{t}^{-2}\\cdot {t}^{3}}{{(1+{t}^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-t}{\\sqrt{(1+{t}^{2})^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we removed the absolute value because $t>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162420/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "814655d8-f459-5df5-b722-3024b87065db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162420"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162388/selection/3cd5dd8ec94a591aa7a9bcdbdd55a93810c8dfced71f47d30ccbaa45ea6e7cf9" :answer/id #uuid "24dc4737-18c4-51be-9132-fdd6e898c958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{(2{e}^{t}+4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162388/selection/c7842211b37a8d01463ca81c7320a57928a469280d1b3605b60bdc1bf7c3b4f2" :answer/id #uuid "a7317bee-4253-5b37-b15a-e40325eb2e33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{({e}^{2t}+4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162388/selection/07ffaf3235ceb9f3cdf978cdaa620ec815dd502025cecbfe41711f549221f1e8" :answer/id #uuid "7ab8076a-8db4-55ef-8c35-4275764f5877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162388/selection/962ea60795191976750f177b35f776e9263fa14f1cc632d5f6c4598ed4c1ca8f" :answer/id #uuid "83c38e27-5ba3-529e-93eb-c4f6cccf291e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162388/selection/93aa51a25bbd97b67c1eed3db41f9cae389d09dc151115ba5ed53f7d49fa6c41" :answer/id #uuid "ac4e130c-d245-583a-9a65-7ae375d21855" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2{e}^{t}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162388/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e9f67dc-8eec-5896-b1ba-e58f7fa904cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162388/selection/c7842211b37a8d01463ca81c7320a57928a469280d1b3605b60bdc1bf7c3b4f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-162388/selection/3cd5dd8ec94a591aa7a9bcdbdd55a93810c8dfced71f47d30ccbaa45ea6e7cf9" "q-162388/selection/c7842211b37a8d01463ca81c7320a57928a469280d1b3605b60bdc1bf7c3b4f2" "q-162388/selection/07ffaf3235ceb9f3cdf978cdaa620ec815dd502025cecbfe41711f549221f1e8" "q-162388/selection/962ea60795191976750f177b35f776e9263fa14f1cc632d5f6c4598ed4c1ca8f" "q-162388/selection/93aa51a25bbd97b67c1eed3db41f9cae389d09dc151115ba5ed53f7d49fa6c41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162388" :question/id #uuid "2d67f4c8-d50b-5861-938e-920000d60dba" :question/math-academy-id "q-162388" :question/problem "The curvature of the plane curve $r(t)={e}^{t}\\,i+2t\\,j$ is given by \n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{}.\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{t},\\,y(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={e}^{t},\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =2 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & ={e}^{t},\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|{e}^{t}\\cdot 0-2\\cdot {e}^{t}|}{{(({e}^{t})^{2}+{2}^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2{e}^{t}|}{{({e}^{2t}+4)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{({e}^{2t}+4)^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162388/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "814655d8-f459-5df5-b722-3024b87065db"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162388"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64901"] :question/problem "Find the radius of the curvature for the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{-t}⟩$ at $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{t},\\,y(t)={e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & ={e}^{t},\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & ={e}^{t},\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & ={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-t}-(-{e}^{-t})\\cdot {e}^{t}|}{{(({e}^{t})^{2}+(-{e}^{-t})^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{({e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t})}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{2}{{({e}^{2(0)}+{e}^{-2(0)})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{2}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{1}{κ(0)}=\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-162425/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1bd0ac98-f093-52d7-a6db-7d23320db589" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162425/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "82ae02f7-0298-50d4-a513-51cb9242ed9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162425/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "06d26735-fa5b-5eaa-a562-a743b4e657df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162425/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2a2aa8a5-1c0c-5388-88f3-25c86fe18f06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162425/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "37de2f4d-2f1c-5289-91ba-51fd2dfbbb1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162425/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "28a0c862-4efc-5e93-a559-abbeab4a0c14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162425/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-162425/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-162425/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-162425/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-162425/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-162425/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162425" :question/id #uuid "36ebf6b1-3a18-5cf6-aafc-2c0ec5515fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162425" :question/problem "Find the radius of the curvature for the curve $r(t)=⟨(1+t)^{2},\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ at $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=(1+t)^{2},\\,y(t)={t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2(1+t),\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =2t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|2(1+t)\\cdot 2-2t\\cdot 2|}{{(\\,(2(1+t))^{2}+(2t)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{8{((1+t)^{2}+{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{1}{2{((1+(0))^{2}+(0)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(1+0)^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{1}{κ(0)}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162425/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36986a18-172c-5983-8f6f-3211b6e8f89d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162403/selection/25e9fb53cfadbd73e90234aa65f80db621ff6adc6ee7ac86a56284fb17a526d8" :answer/id #uuid "9c571bc2-35c7-570d-a288-b1a921ab5fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162403/selection/64f308272685a58f984aadae0d6f02a64a59fbcd1b338d71240ea2ca555ef17b" :answer/id #uuid "c7866a8d-9be9-5327-b333-d494ad8459d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162403/selection/f51ab51d8b5088c4ce66e876eb3f109c990c03237244cc31a4bd31f08e0a2561" :answer/id #uuid "d81299ca-c205-557f-92d3-4842f71314a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162403/selection/5dedd3fc97eb64beda5d906ad6dd87aaae34db54c1ed35ec3a4b810f0ed5b6e3" :answer/id #uuid "73de1ff4-ee8d-51cf-91a8-0c042cc2db9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162403/selection/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980" :answer/id #uuid "880393eb-753a-546c-9dc4-dfe6e16927c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162403/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5012f3a7-3b63-5e7e-b09a-8167a80cfe4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162403/selection/64f308272685a58f984aadae0d6f02a64a59fbcd1b338d71240ea2ca555ef17b" :answer-field/choices ["q-162403/selection/25e9fb53cfadbd73e90234aa65f80db621ff6adc6ee7ac86a56284fb17a526d8" "q-162403/selection/64f308272685a58f984aadae0d6f02a64a59fbcd1b338d71240ea2ca555ef17b" "q-162403/selection/f51ab51d8b5088c4ce66e876eb3f109c990c03237244cc31a4bd31f08e0a2561" "q-162403/selection/5dedd3fc97eb64beda5d906ad6dd87aaae34db54c1ed35ec3a4b810f0ed5b6e3" "q-162403/selection/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162403" :question/id #uuid "49e5c10d-6a90-5598-9eca-de58bdca7cbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-162403" :question/problem "Find the radius of the curvature for the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{2t},\\,{e}^{-t}⟩$ at $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{2t},\\,y(t)={e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2{e}^{2t},\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =4{e}^{2t},\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & ={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|2{e}^{2t}\\cdot {e}^{-t}-(-{e}^{-t})\\cdot 4{e}^{2t}|}{{((2{e}^{2t})^{2}+(-{e}^{-t})^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{e}^{t}}{{(4{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-2t})}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{6{e}^{(0)}}{{(4{e}^{4(0)}+{e}^{-2(0)})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{5}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{1}{κ(0)}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162403/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36986a18-172c-5983-8f6f-3211b6e8f89d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162424/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "88c5cf84-4fcc-577e-9aa5-31603bc7e1d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162424/selection/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer/id #uuid "a79277aa-cbb1-57a1-82d5-8f0b893e94cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162424/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d3ae1406-5c53-5a6e-8f7b-7591ebd60af7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162424/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "c112bad1-a558-5110-8023-22629abc9616" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162424/selection/602764c7df5493d96a41df7b1e43f6b176fc7746e6dea7e7edcd879542478102" :answer/id #uuid "53a23580-64aa-5fd0-bf2a-81839395371c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162424/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b2edb53-5676-5944-8e6f-a77440c922d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162424/selection/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer-field/choices ["q-162424/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-162424/selection/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" "q-162424/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-162424/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-162424/selection/602764c7df5493d96a41df7b1e43f6b176fc7746e6dea7e7edcd879542478102"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162424" :question/id #uuid "cfea61b1-f938-5b31-b11a-e78fec630194" :question/math-academy-id "q-162424" :question/problem "Find the radius of curvature for the curve $r(t)=2{e}^{t}\\,i+{e}^{2t}\\,j$ at $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=2{e}^{t},\\,y(t)={e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2{e}^{t},\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =2{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2{e}^{t},\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|2{e}^{t}\\cdot 4{e}^{2t}-2{e}^{2t}\\cdot 2{e}^{t}|}{{((2{e}^{t})^{2}+(2{e}^{2t})^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{3t}}{{(4{e}^{2t}+4{e}^{4t})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2{(1+{e}^{2t})}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{1}{2{(1+{e}^{2(0)})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2{(1+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{1}{κ(0)}=4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162424/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36986a18-172c-5983-8f6f-3211b6e8f89d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162424"] :db